From 622182053b24b06d147479167b8b525030cf9f38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:49:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Mac Suite: the prompt grows with its text (2 lines min,
 ~40% of the window, then scrolls), expand to a full editor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The composer's prompt box was pinned to 48-72 pt, so a prompt read as one line. It now measures its laid-out text
(NSLayoutManager delegate) and sizes itself between two lines and ~40% of the page height, growing upward (the picture
gives up the height, Generate stays on screen), animated unless Reduce Motion is on. An expand button opens a 760 pt
editor sheet with the same chips and @/# list (⌘Return closes). Extend's prompt grows to 12 lines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Py2rxphub3JG9Gtsd3sf7U
